            "text": "- The test case `test_invalid_json` expects the error message to contain the word \"invalid\", but the actual error message is \"error: input file '/users/argus/optimal-harness/runs/verify-49/work/.harness/commands/cmd-wbiiqvdt/.tmp/tmp4bco8tu3/input.json' is not valid json.\" which does not include \"invalid\". This suggests either the test expectation or the implementation needs to be adjusted to match.\n- The test case `test_non_string_items_in_array` checks for the presence of \"error\" in the stderr, but does not check for specific error messages or ensure that the error message is informative enough to indicate what went wrong.\n- There's no test case for valid input that produces valid output, which would validate the core functionality of the word frequency counter.\n- The test suite does not cover edge cases such as empty strings, whitespace-only strings, or special Unicode characters in the input.\n- There's no test for handling read permissions on input files or handling cases where the output file cannot be written to.\n- The test suite does not validate the format of the output JSON file, particularly whether it adheres to the required structure with `word` and `count` keys in the correct order."
